rategy 2 (Named Lists)  please\n\n# Previous Session Summary:\n# Continuation Summary\n\n## 1. Outstanding User Requests\n- **Auto-Deploy to Surge Rule (Standing Directive):**\n  - *User Directive:* `\"deploy it to surge please...and do so going forward after every new compile\"`\n  - *Status:* **IMPLEMENTATION** (Build and deploy the newly updated web bundle containing the Priority Tier and Named List implementations to `https://valuteachers-dialer.surge.sh`).\n- **Implement Multi-Tier Priority Weighting (Fresh vs. Legacy) + Named Campaign Lists:**\n  - *User Directive:* `\"implement your recommendation for ValuTeachers Workflow, Combining Strategy 1 (Priority Tier toggle on scan) with Strategy 2 (Named Lists) please\"`\n  - *Status:* **IMPLEMENTATION (Code changes complete, ready for compilation/deployment)**.\n\n---\n\n## 2. User Knowledge\n- **Domain & Company:**\n  - Target Company: **ValuTeachers** working with Florida educators on **Florida Retirement System (FRS)**, **D.R.O.P.**, and **403(b)/457(b)** plans.\n  - Primary KPI: **Appointments Set** (`Appt. Set`) — locking in classroom sit-downs during planning periods.\n  - Live Surge Domain: `https://valuteachers-dialer.surge.sh`.\n- **User Directives Verbatim:**\n  - *\"how does it handle it when new leads are added? does it just append them to the end or does it reset the dial count?\"*\n  - *\"do not change the codebase this turn, but suppose i have a bunch of legact lead cards i want to snap into the dialer...they're old and should absolutely be called near the end of the queue. how might we best address incorporating old leads WITHOT+UT messing up the current prioritization of lead calling?\"*\n  - *\"implement your recommendation for ValuTeachers Workflow, Combining Strategy 1 (Priority Tier toggle on scan) with Strategy 2 (Named Lists) please\"*\n  - *\"deploy it to surge please...and do so going forward after every new compile\"*\n\n---\n\n## 3. Work Accomplished\n1. **Schema & Database Updates for Priority Tiers & Lists (`database.ts`, `types/index.ts`):**\n   - Added `priority_tier` property to `Lead` (1 = Fresh/Hot default, 3 = Legacy/Archive) and `ExtractedLeadItem` in `src/types/index.ts`.\n   - Updated `WebDatabase` in `src/db/database.ts` to store `priority_tier`, handle updates, and sort queue queries by `priority_tier ASC, attempts_count ASC, created_at ASC`.\n   - Updated `initNativeDatabase` in `src/db/database.ts` to add `priority_tier INTEGER DEFAULT 1` to SQLite schema and executed `ALTER TABLE leads ADD COLUMN priority_tier INTEGER DEFAULT 1;` migration check.\n2. **Repository Enhancements (`leadsRepository.ts`):**\n   - Updated `createListWithLeads` and `addSingleLead` to accept `priority_tier` and target `list_id`.\n   - Updated `getMasterDialingQueue` and `getDialingQueueForList` with `ORDER BY priority_tier ASC, attempts_count ASC, created_at ASC` so fresh Tier 1 leads are dialed first and legacy Tier 3 leads are placed at the back of the queue.\n   - Added `createNewNamedList(title: string)` and `updateLeadPriority(leadId, priorityTier, listId)` methods.\n   - Updated `hydrateLead` to hydrate `priority_tier` safely.\n3. **Scan Sheet Review & Ingestion Screen (`ScanSheetScreen.tsx`):**\n   - Added interactive **Priority Tier Switcher**:\n     - 🟢 **Fresh / Hot Lead (Tier 1)**: Marked as Priority #1.\n     - 🏛️ **Legacy / Archive (Tier 3)**: Placed at the back of the queue.\n   - Added **Destination Campaign List Selector**:\n     - Allows assigning scanned cards to Master Pipeline, existing custom lists, or creating a new named list (e.g. *\"2023-2024 Legacy Vault\"*) on the fly.\n4. **Pipeline & Campaign Management (`ListsScreen.tsx`):**\n   - Added horizontal **Campaign List & Priority Filter** bar to filter between All Campaigns, specific lists, \"Fresh Only\", or \"Legacy Only\".\n   - Added priority visual badges (🔥 `Fresh` vs 🏛️ `Legacy`) to every lead card.\n   - Updated Power Dialer launch button to dial the currently active campaign list filter.\n5. **Power Dialer HUD (`DialerHudScreen.tsx`):**\n   - Added `🏛️ LEGACY LEAD` vs `🔥 FRESH PRIORITY` indicator badges directly in the educator's HUD profile top ribbon next to the attempt badge.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Model Knowledge\n- **Queue Prioritization Mechanism:**\n  ```sql\n  SELECT * FROM leads \n  WHERE (last_disposition IS NULL OR last_disposition IN ('pending', 'no_answer', 'voicemail'))\n  ORDER BY priority_tier ASC, attempts_count ASC, created_at ASC\n  ```\n  - **Tier 1 (Fresh / Hot):** `priority_tier = 1`. Leads scanned from current cards are dialed first in Round 1.\n  - **Tier 3 (Legacy / Archive):** `priority_tier = 3`. Old legacy cards sit at the very end of the queue and will never jump ahead of fresh leads, regardless of attempt counts.\n- **Custom Campaign Lists:**\n  - Leads can have `list_id = 'master_queue'` or a custom `listId` (e.g., `list_17244...`).\n  - Users can either dial the Master Queue (which sweeps all lists prioritizing Tier 1 -> Tier 3) or dial a specific isolated campaign list from `ListsScreen`.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Files and Code\n\n### Edited Files\n- `src/types/index.ts`: Added `priority_tier` and `list_id` to `Lead` and `ExtractedLeadItem`.\n- `src/db/database.ts`: Added `priority_tier` column definition, migration, and WebDatabase in-memory sorting/storing logic.\n- `src/db/leadsRepository.ts`: Added `priority_tier` persistence, `createNewNamedList`, `updateLeadPriority`, and updated queue sorting queries.\n- `src/screens/ScanSheetScreen.tsx`: Added Priority Tier segmented toggle (Fresh vs Legacy) and Destination Campaign List selection.\n- `src/screens/ListsScreen.tsx`: Added Campaign List filter strip, Priority filter chips (Fresh / Legacy), and priority badges on lead items.\n- `src/screens/DialerHudScreen.tsx`: Added `FRESH PRIORITY` and `LEGACY LEAD` badges to the educator top card in the HUD.\n\n### Viewed Files\n- `src/db/leadsRepository.ts`: Verified `getMasterDialingQueue` (lines 159–167), `getDialingQueueForList` (lines 230–245), and `addSingleLead` (lines 75–140).\n- `src/screens/ScanSheetScreen.tsx`: Reviewed ingestion and review UI (lines 270–380, lines 780–860).\n- `src/screens/ListsScreen.tsx`: Reviewed pipeline list rendering and filters (lines 320–460, lines 760–890).\n- `src/screens/DialerHudScreen.tsx`: Reviewed cockpit top row layout (lines 660–680, lines 1210–1250).\n\n---\n\n## 6. Current Work and Next Steps\n1. **Next Immediate Action:**\n   - Execute the TypeScript type check and export build:\n     ```powershell\n     npx tsc --noEmit\n     npx expo export -p web\n     ```\n   - Deploy the new web bundle to Surge per standing rule:\n     ```powershell\n     npx surge ./dist valuteachers-dialer.surge.sh\n     ```\n2. **User Follow-Up:**\n   - Inform the user that the Fresh vs. Legacy Priority Tiering + Named Lists feature is fully implemented and live on `https://valuteachers-dialer.surge.sh`.\n\nYou have the 4 following artifacts written to the artifacts directory:\n\n[ARTIFACT: media_1787239731075]\nPath: file:///C:/Users/brorm/.gemini/antigravity/brain/9c9b5ef4-82a1-483f-9e9e-cb421c9396b3/.user_uploaded/media_1787239731075.jpg\nLast Edited: 2026-08-20T15:30:15Z\n\n[ARTIFACT: media_1787239731084]\nPath: file:///C:/Users/brorm/.gemini/antigravity/brain/9c9b5ef4-82a1-483f-9e9e-cb421c9396b3/.user_uploaded/media_1787239731084.jpg\nLast Edited: 2026-08-20T15:30:15Z\n\n[ARTIFACT: implementation_plan]\nPath: file:///C:/Users/brorm/.gemini/antigravity/brain/9c9b5ef4-82a1-483f-9e9e-cb421c9396b3/implementation_plan.md\nLast Edited: 2026-08-20T15:30:28Z\n\n[ARTIFACT: walkthrough]\nPath: file:///C:/Users/brorm/.gemini/antigravity/brain/9c9b5ef4-82a1-483f-9e9e-cb421c9396b3/walkthrough.md\nLast Edited: 2026-08-20T22:05:03Z\n\n# Conversation Logs\n\nReference the following log files for the full, untruncated conversation:\n\n- C:\\Users\\brorm\\.gemini\\antigravity\\brain\\9c9b5ef4-82a1-483f-9e9e-cb421c9396b3\\.system_generated\\logs\\transcript.jsonl\n\n**IMPORTANT: t